lt;td&gt;Illinois: 5&lt;/td&gt; &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Michigan: 27&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Illinois: 0&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Michigan: 21&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Oberlin: 2&lt;/td&gt; &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Michigan: 19&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Oberlin: 8&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Michigan: 19&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Denison: 8&lt;/td&gt; &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Michigan: 22&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Denison: 5&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="individual-results-2"&gt;Individual Results&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Men&amp;rsquo;s Epee: &lt;strong&gt;Ethan Madison&lt;/strong&gt;, 🥉&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Women&amp;rsquo;s Epee: &lt;strong&gt;Amina Troupe&lt;/strong&gt;, 🥈; &lt;strong&gt;Faith Chang&lt;/strong&gt;, 🥉; &lt;strong&gt;Phoenix Williams&lt;/strong&gt;, 🥉&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Women&amp;rsquo;s Foil: &lt;strong&gt;Molly Cavanaugh&lt;/strong&gt;, 🥉&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item><item><title>Mass Meeting Tomorrow</title><link>https://www.um-fencing.com/email-archive/members-fencing_mass_meeting_tomorrow-20180909/</link><pubDate>Sun, 09 Sep 2018 17:00:51 -0400</pubDate><guid>https://www.um-fencing.com/email-archive/members-fencing_mass_meeting_tomorrow-20180909/</guid><description>&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;From: Zachary Zipper &amp;lt;zezip@umich.edu&amp;gt;&#10;Date: Sun, 9 Sep 2018 17:00:51 -0400&#10;Subject: Fencing Mass Meeting Tomorrow&#10;To: University of Michigan Fencing Club Members &amp;lt;fencing-club@umich.edu&amp;gt;&#10;Cc: Fencing Officers &amp;lt;fencingofficers@umich.edu&amp;gt;&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;Dear All,&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We are holding our mass meeting at the Coliseum tomorrow.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;As returning members of the club, feel free to set up strips and start&#10;fencing on the opposite side of the gym. This will make good use of&#10;practice time and allow newbies to walk in and immediately see some fencing&#10;in real life.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Welcome to U-M Fencing!</title><link>https://www.um-fencing.com/welcome/</link><pubDate>Sun, 21 Jan 2018 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.um-fencing.com/welcome/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the University of Michigan Fencing team!&#10;Whether you&amp;rsquo;re a new or returning member, we look forward to having you.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This page will be helpful to you in (re)joining the club, receiving all important information throughout the year, and getting to know your teammates.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="becoming-a-member"&gt;Becoming a Member&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Please follow these steps to become a member of the club this term. &lt;em&gt;All members, including those returning, must complete these annually!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Add Our Calendar</title><link>https://www.um-fencing.com/add_calendar/</link><pubDate>Wed, 24 Aug 2016 15:35:56 -0400</pubDate><guid>https://www.um-fencing.com/add_calendar/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="to-add-the-umfc-calendar-to-google-calendar"&gt;To add the UMFC calendar to Google Calendar:&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ol&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Visit &lt;a target="_blank" href="[https://calendar.googe.com](https://calendar.google.com/calendar/u/1?cid=Y19mMjljZDZkNTZiZDE2ZWFkMTY1YTgzMjBkNGVlZjVlNDdiZDMxMGZjMDA2M2JhYTVhZWUxZGVjYjg5NTU2MzM5QGdyb3VwLmNhbGVuZGFyLmdvb2dsZS5jb20)"&gt;Google Calendar&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Click on &amp;ldquo;Add Calendar&amp;rdquo;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ol&gt;</description></item><item><title>Donate</title><link>https://www.um-fencing.com/donate/</link><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jun 2016 14:49:10 -0700</pubDate><guid>https://www.um-fencing.com/donate/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The University of Michigan Fencing Club is excited about the upcoming season.&#10;We are not only eager to defend our title as the USACFC national champions, but we want everyone on campus to have the opportunity to join our club, learn how to fence, and take fencing with them for the rest of their lives.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;One of our top priorities is investing in the future to create a growing and sustainable organization.&#10;With your help we can continue to compete at the highest level while offering the beginning of a lifelong experience for UofM students.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>About Fencing</title><link>https://www.um-fencing.com/about_fencing/</link><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jun 2016 14:07:29 -0700</pubDate><guid>https://www.um-fencing.com/about_fencing/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The sport of fencing has three weapons: foil, epee and saber.&#10;The object of a fencing bout (what an individual &amp;ldquo;game&amp;rdquo; is called) is to land a specified number of touches on your opponent before he/she scores that number on you.&#10;Each bout is officiated by a referee called a director.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="electric-scoring"&gt;Electric Scoring&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;All official tournaments are conducted using electric scoring systems.&#10;The fencers connect themselves, their blades, and their metal jackets (lames) to a retractable cord (reel), which plugs in to a scoring machine (pictured left).&#10;The machine shows a light for each fencer who successfully scores a touch on his or her opponent.&#10;The director then describes the action and awards points based on right-of-way.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Join</title><link>https://www.um-fencing.com/join/</link><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jun 2016 14:00:17 -0700</pubDate><guid>https://www.um-fencing.com/join/</guid><description>&lt;div class="alert alert-info" role="alert"&gt;&#13;&#10; Already attended a practice? See the &lt;a href="../welcome"&gt;welcome&lt;/a&gt; page for the next steps towards becoming a member.&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;p&gt;No experience is necessary, and all equipment is provided by the team!&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We have a Mass Meeting early each Fall for interested newcomers.&#10;Look for our booths at Rec Sports Expo and at Festifall for more information.&#10;If you cannot attend the Mass Meeting, simply attend any practice.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;If you&amp;rsquo;re joining us later or haven&amp;rsquo;t been receiving emails, please check the &lt;a href="../email-archive/"&gt;archive&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Contact</title><link>https://www.um-fencing.com/contact/</link><pubDate>Mon, 27 Jun 2016 15:09:24 -0700</pubDate><guid>https://www.um-fencing.com/contact/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;We&amp;rsquo;d love to hear from you! If you have a question, you can ask any of our officers at practice or contact us electronically.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="container-fluid"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="row"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="col-md-6"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="alert alert-info" role="alert"&gt;&#13;&#10; Have general inquiry questions?&#10;Email us at &lt;a href="mailto:fencingofficers@umich.edu"&gt;fencingofficers@umich.edu&lt;/a&gt;.&#10;We can help in person, too. Stop by during any practice and we&amp;rsquo;ll take care of you.&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="col-md-6"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="alert alert-info" role="alert"&gt;&#13;&#10; Want to anonymously give feedback, ask a question, raise a concern, etc.?&#10;Please use our &lt;a href="https://forms.gle/jgLxrP3zrSTAueLGA"&gt;suggestions box&lt;/a&gt;.&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="officers"&gt;Officers&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;table&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;Position&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;Name&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;Email Address&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;Contact About&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/thead&gt;&#1